This is an altered Pyxis port. Local changes are recorded in the recipe's
ordered patches/ series. The recipe's Makefile and pyxis_config.h define the
static build; upstream's default configuration is disabled. LICENSE contains
the upstream raylib license. THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES contains the selected bundled
component licenses and notices reached by this profile. Preserve upstream
source notices when distributing source.

Compiled translation units: rcore, rshapes, rtextures, rtext and rmodels.
Renderer/platform: GRAPHICS_API_OPENGL_SOFTWARE (bundled rlsw 1.6), SDL2.
SDL2 is a separate build/link dependency with separately distributed notices.
No OpenGL driver, GLAD, GLFW, X11 or GPU library is selected by this profile.

Enabled: 2D shapes, image generation and manipulation, PNG decoding, default
font and TrueType/OpenType font loading through stb_truetype, direct basic-3D
drawing, camera helpers, compression and pseudo-random-number helpers. The
bundled reached dependencies are rlsw, rprand (including Xoshiro128** and
SplitMix64), sinfl, sdefl, stb_image, stb_image_resize2, stb_perlin,
stb_rect_pack and stb_truetype. The raymath and rcamera header notices are
also retained. rlsw SIMD is disabled in this initial profile.

Omitted: raudio, miniaudio and audio decoders; every image decoder except PNG;
compressed texture containers; image export; FNT/BDF font loaders; external
model/animation format loaders; mesh generation; GPU skinning; gestures,
automation, screenshot hotkeys and clipboard-image loading. External font,
image and other application assets are not supplied or licensed by this port.

Software rendering does not provide GLSL/compute, compressed-texture or GPU
capabilities. Source selection and successful compilation/linking do not
qualify display layout, scaling, input, timing, render-texture combinations
or visual/basic-3D correctness on Pyxis. Runtime qualification is a separate
integration task. Applications must use explicitly delegated asset roots;
this port supplies no authority to infer or access private project locations.
